  "instance_name": "anti_black_stereotype_of_physical_appearance",
  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Physical Appearance",
  "description": "The meme implicitly references the stereotype that Black women are often hypersexualized or objectified based on their physical appearance, particularly their body size. The image of a Black woman on a beach, combined with the text 'i don't like the sun so i wear a visor,' can be read as a punchline that plays on the stereotype that Black women are 'too hot' or 'too dark' to be on the beach, thus needing to 'hide' or 'avoid' the sun. This is a form of racialized body shaming that ties into broader anti-Black stereotypes about physicality and behavior.",
